2. gridfm-datakit (Apache-2.0)
   https://github.com/gridfm/gridfm-datakit, pinned commit
   d8a092dcfdcc05f58f12595e9f7a9fd165d3c2f0 (main, 2026-10-01).
   Used to generate the stress, calibration and exhaustive N-1 scenario sets
   (configs/datakit/) and by scripts/gen_exhaustive_gen_outages.py, which
   imports its generator. It runs Julia PowerModels.jl and Ipopt for the
   AC power-flow solves; those are separate projects with their own licenses.
   Copyright the gridfm-datakit authors (IBM Research and contributors).

3. GENCO paper and released artifacts
   "GENCO: a grid foundation model architecture for power flow, optimal power
   flow and state estimation", arXiv:2608.09921 (2026), IBM Research,
   Hydro-Quebec, ETH Zurich and Stony Brook University.
   - Checkpoints and normalizer statistics: Hugging Face model repos
     gridfm/genco-pf-datakit and gridfm/genco-opf-datakit (model card:
     Apache-2.0). Fetched at run time by scripts/fetch_data.py,
     scripts/reproduce.py, scripts/build_basecase_store.py and
     src/genco_certified/loading.py. They are not redistributed here.
   - Datasets: Hugging Face dataset repos gridfm/pf_small_<grid> and
     gridfm/opf_small_<grid> (datakit-generated scenarios), fetched by
     scripts/fetch_data.py. Not redistributed here, except a small subset of
     IEEE 118 scenarios bundled in space/bundle/ for the demo Space. Their terms
     are those on the dataset cards; check them before redistributing.
   - Challenge: GridFM GENCO Challenge 2026
     (https://huggingface.co/spaces/gridfm/genco-challenge).

4. Network cases
   IEEE 14, 30, 57 and 118-bus systems and the GOC 500 / 2000 / 10000 cases are
   taken through datakit's PGLib-OPF / MATPOWER case files (PGLib-OPF,
   IEEE PES Task Force on Benchmarks for Validation of Emerging Power System
   Algorithms, CC BY 4.0; MATPOWER, BSD-3-Clause). We do not ship the case files
   themselves; the bundled demo scenarios contain derived data only.

5. Python dependencies
   PyTorch, PyTorch Geometric, torch-scatter, Lightning, SciPy, NumPy, pandas,
   PyArrow, scikit-learn, Gradio and others, under their own licenses; the
   exact versions are in requirements.lock.txt and results/environment.json.
